 in Building 7, Room 408, with free admission.","source_url":"https://arts.mit.edu/exhibitions/","source_title":"Exhibitions | MIT Arts","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"MIT lists hours as Monday–Sunday, 9:00 a.m.–6:00 p.m.; verify before travel.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mit-koch-public-galleries","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Koch Institute Public Galleries","title":"Explore biomedical images and research","subtitle":"MIT Koch Institute, Cambridge","notes":"Visit the public galleries together, read the project displays, and pick one image or research question to discuss on the way out.","short_summary":"MIT’s public galleries connect visitors with biomedical images and cancer-research projects.","evidence_claim":"MIT Arts describes the Koch Institute Public Galleries as spaces for visitors to explore current cancer research, biomedical images, and related contexts; its exhibitions page identifies the gallery offerings as free admission.","source_url":"https://arts.mit.edu/exhibitions/","source_title":"Exhibitions | MIT Arts","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Review MIT’s current exhibition information before visiting campus.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"massart-art-museum","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"MassArt Art Museum","title":"Reserve a free MAAM visit","subtitle":"621 Huntington Avenue, Boston","notes":"Reserve a no-cost timed ticket, then use the gallery visit as a focused afternoon activity with time afterward to talk about the work.","short_summary":"MassArt’s teaching museum presents contemporary art with free admission.","evidence_claim":"MassArt Art Museum states that it is always free and offers free tickets for visits.","source_url":"https://maam.massart.edu/alwaysfree","source_title":"Always Free! | MassArt Art Museum","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Advance ticket registration is recommended; the museum notes that tickets can sell out.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"arnold-arboretum","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Arnold Arboretum of Harvard University","title":"Take a self-guided plant walk","subtitle":"125 Arborway, Boston","notes":"Choose a self-guided tour from the Arboretum’s visitor page, walk the marked landscape together, and stay on paths while observing plants and wildlife.","short_summary":"A large living collection with free daily landscape access and self-guided routes.","evidence_claim":"The Arnold Arboretum states that its 281-acre landscape is open daily and free for all to explore, with admission always free.","source_url":"https://arboretum.harvard.edu/visit/","source_title":"Visit | Arnold Arboretum of Harvard University","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Landscape access is daily from sunrise to sunset; follow posted visitor guidelines.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uss-constitution-ship","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"USS Constitution","title":"Board USS Constitution","subtitle":"Charlestown Navy Yard, Boston","notes":"Bring required government photo ID if 18 or older, allow time for security screening, and board on a first-come basis during ship visiting hours.","short_summary":"A free, first-come visit aboard the active historic Navy ship.","evidence_claim":"USS Constitution Museum states that the ship is free to visit on a first-come, first-served basis.","source_url":"https://ussconstitutionmuseum.org/hours-admission/","source_title":"Hours + Admission | USS Constitution Museum","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The ship is open Wednesday–Sunday, 10:00 a.m.–6:00 p.m.; security screening is required, and visitors 18+ need federal or state photo ID.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
